THE lcm-OUTLIER MECHANISM: base {1..N-2} covers d=2..N-2; the two missing divisors are d=N-1, d=N;
the minimal single speed carrying BOTH is lcm(N-1,N) = (N-1)N. So the min single-outlier covering
family is {1..N-2, (N-1)N}, and on the ladder that outlier is rung k=N = the first covering rung.

 N | base {1..N-2} missing | lcm(N-1,N)=(N-1)N | family {1..N-2,(N-1)N} covering? | M | =N/Phi6(N)?
 3 |             [2, 3] |              6=6 |                         True |     3/7 | True
