CHECK the minimality: is (N-1)N the SMALLEST outlier making {1..N-2, w} covering? (need mult of N-1 AND N)
 N | smallest w with {1..N-2,w} covering | = (N-1)N? | (any single w<(N-1)N covering?)
 3 |                                    6 |      True | no single w below (N-1)N covers both N-1 and N
 4 |                                   12 |      True | no single w below (N-1)N covers both N-1 and N
 5 |                                   20 |      True | no single w below (N-1)N covers both N-1 and N
