=> The covering-min single-outlier family is {1..N-2, lcm(N-1,N)} = {1..N-2,(N-1)N}, the first
   covering rung k=N of the ladder, M=N/Phi6(N). klein's 182=13*14=lcm(13,14) is the N=14 instance.
   (Whether a MULTI-outlier / compressed family beats it: small N yes {2,3}/{1,3,4}; N=14 no, klein ILP.)
